<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermigar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/429">429</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermigar was a king of the Suebi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in the early 5th century. In 429, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> under Gaiseric prepared to cross to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, his Suebi were plundering Lusitania; the Vandals defeated him near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerita-augusta">Emerita Augusta</a> (Mérida), and he drowned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> while fleeing. The episode is recorded by the chronicler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hydatius">Hydatius</a>.</p></div>
